  "title": "Remove Duplicate Refund Requests Keeping Latest",
  "prompt": "Your e-commerce platform's `refund_requests` table has accumulated duplicates when customers accidentally submitted the same refund request multiple times for the same order line item. Business rules require keeping only the most recent request (highest `request_id`) for each unique combination of `order_id` and `line_item_id`, and deleting all earlier duplicates. Write a single DELETE statement that removes these duplicate refund requests, preserving only the latest one per order line item. After the deletion, return all remaining rows ordered by `request_id` ascending to confirm the cleanup.",
