  "hints": [
    "You need to identify which refund requests are duplicates for the same order line item.",
    "For each (order_id, line_item_id) pair, keep only the row with the maximum request_id and delete all others.",
    "Use a correlated subquery in the WHERE clause that compares each row's request_id against the MAX(request_id) for its group: DELETE FROM refund_requests WHERE request_id < (SELECT MAX(...) WHERE order_id = ... AND line_item_id = ...)."
  ],
  "answer_key": "DELETE FROM refund_requests WHERE request_id < (SELECT MAX(r2.request_id) FROM refund_requests r2 WHERE r2.order_id = refund_requests.order_id AND r2.line_item_id = refund_requests.line_item_id);\nSELECT * FROM refund_requests ORDER BY request_id;",
